body='''<div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Native admission v0.1 · development</div><h1>Test the operator before the bridge.</h1><p class="lede">The declared native spectra impose a residual floor on the full programmed clock. Copies and a common rate adjustment cannot produce exact generator agreement. An endpoint can still match through phase aliasing.</p></div>
<aside class="callout"><strong>Exact conditional spectral audit · physical promotion 0</strong><p>The comparison uses the three frozen unit-metric carriers. Adjustable metrics, coupled or differently scaled copies and new source operators require separate premises. The free scale below is a comparison control, not a derived native parameter.</p></aside>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Compare the signed spectral classes</h2><div class="search-tools"><label>Native class<select id="na-class"><option value="tetra">Filled tetrahedron · Δ³</option><option value="minus">Two-cell face join · K−</option><option value="plus">Three-cell edge join · K+</option></select></label><label>Even clock length<select id="na-length"><option>2</option><option>4</option><option>6</option><option>8</option><option selected>10</option><option>12</option></select></label></div><p>The published programme uses n=10. Other lengths inspect the abstract spin-clock spectral family, with no revised payload programme implied. Positive frequencies are shown; negative modes mirror them.</p><div class="jc-controls"><label>High native centre / κ <output id="na-scale-label"></output><input type="range" id="na-scale" min="0" max="20" step="any" value="7"></label><button type="button" id="na-best">Best comparison witness</button></div><p id="na-verdict" role="status"></p><div id="na-spectrum"></div><div id="na-summary"></div><div id="na-gaps"></div><details><summary>Exact ordered-partition certificates</summary><div id="na-certificates"></div></details></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>A large residual can coexist with an exact endpoint</h2><p>For the n=10 clock, an engineered encoding into five tetrahedral copies per data label matches every endpoint eigenphase at T=π/(2κ). Its generator residual is 8κ, while complete endpoint channel discrepancy is exactly zero. Intermediate propagation differs.</p><div id="na-alias"></div><p>A lower floor on Tη prevents this particular Duhamel budget from certifying small error. It supplies no lower bound on actual error or failure probability. The endpoint alias preserves that distinction.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>What can enter the next native test?</h2><p>A source-authored geometry, metric or coupling can change the spectral class. It needs a complete encoding E, prepared bank and clock, source-defined rate and readout, and protected record retention. Choosing weights or a rate to match a target is not that source law.</p><p>An explicitly weaker prepared-window or endpoint contract is another route. It must retain the complete state and its acquisition costs. The exact full-generator result and the closed-factor no-go remain scoped to their declared assumptions.</p><p>Independent human review and physical calibration remain open. This is development, with no registry entry or CRL promotion.</p></div></section>
<noscript><p>The comparison inspector requires JavaScript. The exact proof and replay below contain all certificates.</p></noscript><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/releases/UD_NATIVE_SPECTRAL_ADMISSION_v0.1.zip" download>Download native audit and replay ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/native-admission-v0.1/UD_NATIVE_SPECTRAL_ADMISSION_v0.1.md">Theorems and proof</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/native-admission-v0.1/NATIVE_ADMISSION_ROOT_VERIFICATION_v0.1.json">Root receipt</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/native-admission-v0.1/native-admission-source-review.md">AI source/scope review</a><a class="text-link" href="/programmed-clock/">Programmed clock</a></div>'''
